---
description: After SQL migration changes, run db:migrate; on failure fix SQL and retry until success
globs: supabase/migrations/**/*.sql
alwaysApply: false
---

# DB migrations — run, fix, retry

When you **create or materially edit** a file in `supabase/migrations/`:

1. Use the next sequential prefix. Prefer idempotent SQL.
2. Run `npm run db:migrate` from project root. Do not ask the user to paste SQL.
3. On failure, fix the pending SQL and retry until success or a real env/network blocker (missing `SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD` / `DATABASE_URL` in `.env.local`).

Report applied filenames (or `No pending migrations.`) to the user.
